  clock: 16  # f5d7
  nonce: f5d7  # f5d7
  message: "PROMOTED P1 -> P0 ON EXPLICIT OWNER AUTHORISATION, 2026-08-21. Recorded here in\nthe owner's terms because a rank change that lives only in conversation is\nindistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE AUTHORISATION. Presented with the isolating repro recorded above -- the\nunannotated-receiver arm returning \"This service never sends data over the\nnetwork. Verdict: confirmed\" for a function whose entire body is\nsock.sendall(payload), with the fs_read control firing violated in BOTH arms --\nthe owner selected \"Promote to P0 and fix\", and referred back to the standing\ninstruction on this item: if it becomes P0, that is \"not a reason to stop and\nreport, it is a reason to go deeper\" and FIX it.\n\nWHY THE PROMOTION IS EARNED NOW AND WAS NOT BEFORE. The 2026-08-20 owner\ninterview authorised a repro SEARCH under three conditions, and named the\nblocker precisely: this item was \"a LIVE DEFECT WITH NO LIVE REPRO\", which \"is\nthe shape that gets items falsely closed\". That blocker is gone. Condition (1),\ncheck the assumptions before hunting, is what removed it: the item's own title\npremise was stale, and the fixture the thread already contained reproduces at\ndev 09921c57a1 in about two minutes of the timebox opened at 19:15 UTC.\n\nSo what changed is not the severity of the defect -- it was always a security\ntool certifying absence it could not establish -- but that it is now\nDEMONSTRABLE in six lines, with a control, on stdlib only, with no overlay and\nno opaque launch to argue about.\n\nWHAT THE FIX MUST AND MUST NOT BE, from this thread's own measurements:\n  * NOT the method-name gate as previously proposed. It blanket-downgrades on\n    real repos (poetry: every boundary, db_read 234 / ipc_recv 160 / fs_read 93\n    / ...) because catalogued method names include close/get/read/write/send.\n    That half of the refutation is intact.\n  * The OTHER half of that refutation does NOT survive and should not be cited:\n    it was argued from session.post, a primitive absent from the catalogue\n    entirely (INV-fotav's third-party gap), not one reached through an untyped\n    receiver. sendall IS catalogued (python.yaml net_send, socket.socket\n    methods), so the \"anti-correlated with the truth\" finding does not apply to\n    the shape this item is about.\n  * Interprocedural argument typing is the sound RECALL fix and remains\n    sequenced behind precision by the <50% band.\n  * The statement of THIS item is a COVERAGE-HONESTY statement, not a recall\n    one: \"Every clean (zero-chain) boundary verdict reported as confirmed must\n    be backed by an analysis that could have classified the I/O.\" A fix that\n    makes the verdict honest satisfies the statement; a fix that makes the flow\n    visible satisfies a different and larger one.\n\nFix work begins under this authorisation. Status stays violated until there is\nbehavioural evidence on the two-arm repro, per the closure-evidence discipline."  # f5d7
- op: discuss  # 2edb
  at: '2026-08-21T19:40:08Z'  # 2edb
  by: agent  # 2edb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2edb
  clock: 17  # 2edb
  nonce: 2edb  # 2edb
  message: "FIX DESIGN, chosen against this thread's own refutations and the module's\nexisting precedent. Recorded before implementation so the reasoning is\nreviewable separately from the diff.\n\nTHE SHAPE: A NEW CAVEAT KIND, NOT A DOWNGRADE. When a boundary claim would come\nback `confirmed` on zero chains, and the edge set contains call sites whose\nreceiver the analysis could not type AND whose callee name is catalogued as a\nmethod-kind primitive FOR THE BOUNDARY UNDER CLAIM, the verdict becomes\n`confirmed_with_caveats` carrying a new `untyped_receiver` caveat that NAMES the\nsites. Exit 3.\n\nWHY THIS DISSOLVES THE 2026-08-11 REFUTATION RATHER THAN IGNORING IT. That entry\nmeasured the proposed finer signal and recorded DO NOT BUILD IT, on the ground\nthat it \"blanket-downgrades on real repos\" -- poetry, every boundary, db_read\n234 / ipc_recv 160 / fs_read 93 / net_send 37. That objection is aimed at a\nDOWNGRADE TO `inconclusive`, and it is correct about that: PR #251 had already\nrejected sending every repo to inconclusive because it tells the reader nothing.\nA caveat is not that. The claim still HOLDS; what changes is that the verdict\nstops being silent about what it could not examine.\n\nAND THE MODULE HAS ALREADY MADE THIS EXACT ARGUMENT, for the sibling case.\nCAVEAT_OPAQUE_BOUNDARY's own docstring in verify_claims.py:\n\n    \"WHY THIS IS NOT `inconclusive`. That verdict conflated two states: 'a whole\n     language here has no catalogue, I am blind' and 'I examined every call and\n     understood them all; three hand control to git/pip/rustup and no static\n     tool can see inside a launched process'. The auditor distinction is exact\n     -- a DISCLAIMER versus a QUALIFIED OPINION.\"\n\nUntyped receivers are the same distinction one step over. \"I have no catalogue\nfor this language\" is a disclaimer. \"I saw this call, I know `sendall` is a\ncatalogued net_send method, and I could not determine the receiver's type\" is a\nqualified opinion. The fourth verdict exists for exactly that, and ADR-0016\nsection 4's original wording for it -- \"consistent, but opaque boundaries exist\nthat could not be verified\" -- reads onto this case without strain.\n\nSO THIS IS THE THIRD MEMBER OF AN ESTABLISHED FAMILY, not a new mechanism:\n  user_supplied_sanitizer  (INV-faput)  the repo vouched for itself\n  opaque_boundary          (ADR-0016)   control left the process\n  untyped_receiver         (INV-fibis)  the receiver could not be typed\n\nBOUNDARY-SCOPED IS LOAD-BEARING. The caveat must be raised only for names\ncatalogued for THE CLAIMED boundary, not for any catalogued name. That is what\nkeeps a dict `.get` out of a net_send verdict -- the specific mis-fire the\n2026-08-11 measurement caught (\"`net_send` would stay CONFIRMABLE while db_read\nand ipc_recv downgrade on an unrelated dict .get\"). Scoping inverts that\nexample: the unrelated `.get` cannot touch the net_send claim at all.\n\nEXIT-CODE CONSEQUENCE, stated rather than discovered later. Repos that today\nexit 0 on such a claim will exit 3. That is deliberate and already documented as\nfail-closed: a gate written `verify-claims ... || exit 1` fails on exit 3 where\nit previously passed (INV-pojib). For a tool whose failure mode here is\ncertifying absence it could not establish, fail-closed is the correct default.\n\nWHAT MUST BE MEASURED BEFORE MERGE, per the standing rule and this item's own\nhistory:\n  * The two-arm repro must move: ARM 1 (unannotated) from `confirmed` to\n    `confirmed_with_caveats` naming sock.sendall; ARM 2 (annotated) unchanged at\n    `violated`; CONTROL-FSREAD unchanged at `violated` in both arms.\n  * A corpus pass reading BOTH directions -- how many verdicts move confirmed ->\n    confirmed_with_caveats, and (the direction nobody looks at) whether any\n    `violated` verdict is disturbed. It must not be.\n  * hypergumbo's own 18 self-claims: any movement there is a claim-surface\n    change and reds the self-claims gate, which now runs on every code PR\n    (INV-bobor). Expect movement and check the snapshot deliberately rather than\n    re-recording it.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE, and named so it is not mistaken for part of this: making the flow\nVISIBLE (interprocedural argument typing) remains the sound recall fix and stays\nsequenced behind precision by the <50% band. This makes the VERDICT honest; it\ndoes not make the analysis see further."  # 2edb
- op: discuss  # 380b
  at: '2026-08-22T07:39:19Z'  # 380b
  by: agent  # 380b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 380b
  clock: 18  # 380b
  nonce: 380b  # 380b
  message: "RECEIVER-TYPING HALF SHIPPED, PR #477 (dev 467027eafa). Status stays violated\npending an owner ruling, and the reason is in the second paragraph rather than\nburied: the change does what this item asked on its own filed repro and moves\nNOTHING on three real repositories.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO MOVES AS THIS ITEM REQUIRED. Three arms differing only in the\nannotation and in whether a call site exists:\n    unannotated + a call site    inconclusive -> VIOLATED, 1 net_send chain\n    annotated                    violated, 1 net_send chain      (unchanged)\n    unannotated, NO call site    confirmed_with_caveats          (unchanged)\nThe third arm is the control: with nothing to infer from, PR #471's\nuntyped_receiver caveat correctly still fires rather than the new pass inventing\na type.\n\n*** AND THE CORPUS MEASURED THE EFFECT AT ZERO. *** A/B on poetry, mitmproxy and\npretix -- arms differing only in this pass, two claim files each (ten boundary\nclaims plus the six generic taint claims) -- produced BYTE-IDENTICAL output in\nall twelve runs. Not 'no regressions'. No change.\n\nThe pass is NOT inert, which is a separate measurement and the one that\ndistinguishes 'works, no catalogue coverage' from 'does not work': mitmproxy's\nunresolved method-call edges go external 6541 -> 6526, typed 2237 -> 2252, i.e.\n+15 strictly better typed with the total unchanged at 8778. Not one newly-typed\nmodule is in the io_primitives catalogue (mitmproxy.http.Headers,\nargparse.ArgumentParser, django.core.mail.SafeMIMEMultipart, collections.Counter,\nrest_framework.test.APIClient), so nothing propagates to a boundary or a verdict.\n\nWHY THE REACH IS SMALL, measured rather than guessed. Of the hints the pass\nagrees on: poetry 18, of which **18 are on parameters that ALREADY carry an\nannotation**; mitmproxy 13 (8 annotated); pretix 51 (22 annotated, 17 on a\nparameter that is never a method receiver). The annotation always wins, so a\nwell-typed codebase leaves this pass nothing to do. That is correct behaviour\nand it is why the corpus zero is not evidence of a defect.\n\nFOR THE <50% BAND: a recall widening that adds ZERO reported findings cannot\nhave added a false one, which is the strongest available answer to the band's\nconcern. It is equally a statement that the payoff is LATENT rather than\ndemonstrated.\n\n*** ONE PREMISE ON THIS ITEM IS NARROWER THAN RECORDED, and whoever rules on\nclosure needs it. *** The session.post shape cannot actually produce a false\n in a repository that imports requests at all: INV-fotav's\nuncovered-module disclosure fires on the IMPORT, so the verdict is already\n before receiver typing is reached. Verified on a fixture in both\narms -- pre-change names 1 uncatalogued module (requests), post-change names 2\n(requests, requests.Session). The verdict does not move; what improves is that\nthe disclosure now names the RECEIVER TYPE, which is the string a user needs to\nwrite an overlay. So the exposure this item framed around session.post is\nsmaller than it reads, and the sock.sendall shape -- where the module IS\ncatalogued -- was the one that mattered. Both halves of that are now addressed:\nPR #471 discloses it, PR #477 sees through it.\n\nTHE CORPUS CAUGHT A DEFECT REVIEW DID NOT, and the first cut had it wrong.\nResolving an argument expression through import bindings alone asserts that\nx = json.dumps(y) names a TYPE -- identical AST shape to s = socket.socket().\nMeasured on poetry: 7 of 19 agreed hints (37%) were FUNCTION RESULTS. Not merely\nuseless: io_boundary._module_matches does bidirectional SUBSTRING matching, so\njson.dumps in a module slot can match a catalogue module  and mint a\nconfident false boundary plus a false taint sink -- the exact class WI-zilag\ndocuments. The gate is now catalogue-first (WI-fuvuj's binding-checked\n_external_constructor_type, which admits lowercase socket.socket) then PascalCase\n(PEP 8's class convention, which is what admits requests.Session).\n\nWHAT REMAINS OPEN, for the ruling: this item's statement is about a clean\nboundary verdict being backed by an analysis that COULD have classified the I/O.\nPR #471 made the verdict disclose untyped receivers; PR #477 types a subset of\nthem. Whether that satisfies the statement, or whether the zero corpus movement\nmeans it does not, is a scope judgement I am not making unilaterally."  # 380b
- op: discuss  # 6c8c
  at: '2026-08-22T07:39:40Z'  # 6c8c
  by: agent  # 6c8c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6c8c
  clock: 19  # 6c8c
  nonce: 6c8c  # 6c8c
  message: "CORRECTION to the entry immediately above: three words were eaten by shell\ncommand substitution (backticks in a double-quoted argument) before the message\nwas stored. The elisions and their restorations, so no reader has to guess:\n\n  1. \"cannot actually produce a false ___ in a repository that imports requests\n     at all\"                                                 -> CONFIRMED\n  2. \"so the verdict is already ___ before receiver typing is reached\"\n                                                             -> INCONCLUSIVE\n  3. \"so ___.dumps in a module slot can match a catalogue module\"\n                                                             -> JSON\n\nNo number or claim in that entry is affected; three nouns went missing and two\nsentences lost the verdict word that carried their point. The tooling note is\nalready on the record elsewhere and applies here: `tracker discuss` takes its\nmessage as an ARGUMENT, so it must be built from a QUOTED heredoc into a\nvariable and passed as \"$MSG\" -- exactly the way this correction was."  # 6c8c
- op: discuss  # 5aa2
  at: '2026-08-22T20:05:48Z'  # 5aa2
  by: agent  # 5aa2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5aa2
  clock: 20  # 5aa2
  nonce: 5aa2  # 5aa2
  message: "*** CORRECTION: A CLAIM I RECORDED ON THIS ITEM YESTERDAY IS FALSE. *** Caught by\na 3-judge panel and re-verified by me before recording this.\n\nTHE FALSE CLAIM, from the 2026-08-22 entry above, in my own words:\n\n  \"The session.post shape cannot actually produce a false CONFIRMED in a\n   repository that imports requests at all: INV-fotav's uncovered-module\n   disclosure fires on the IMPORT, so the verdict is already INCONCLUSIVE\n   before receiver typing is reached.\"\n\nThat is wrong. Three one-file fixtures, each with \"import requests\" present,\none net_send must_not_exist claim, run at HEAD:\n\n    import requests; requests.post(url, data={})                 -> inconclusive  rc 2\n    def upload(session: requests.Session, url): session.post(..) -> inconclusive  rc 2\n    def upload(session, url):                   session.post(..) -> CONFIRMED    rc 0\n\nThe gate keys on the RESOLVED RECEIVER TYPE at the call site, not on the\nimport. So the exposure is WIDER than I recorded, not narrower, and the\nmitigating sentence should be struck rather than qualified.\n\nHOW I GOT IT WRONG, because the shape of the error matters more than the fact:\nI tested ONE fixture -- the direct requests.post form -- observed inconclusive\nin both arms, and generalised to the whole shape without running the\nunannotated-parameter form, which is the one this item is actually about. A\none-arm test of the wrong arm. The project's own rule 13 covers this exactly:\na comfortable result is a claim, and it needs the control that discriminates.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES TO THE ITEM. The 2026-08-22 entry drew two conclusions from that\npremise: (1) that session.post's exposure is smaller than the item's text\nimplies, and (2) that \"the sock.sendall shape -- where the module IS catalogued\n-- was the one that mattered\". Conclusion (1) IS WITHDRAWN. Conclusion (2)\nsurvives but for a different reason than I gave: sendall matters because it is\ncatalogued, not because session.post was harmless.\n\nA SEPARATE FINDING FROM THE SAME PANEL, filed as INV-jujoh (P0) rather than\nfolded here: a call whose receiver is an OWN INSTANCE FIELD of external or\nunknown type emits NO EDGE AT ALL, so a bare confirmed is returned even for a\nCATALOGUED stdlib primitive with the type known. That is upstream of every\nmechanism this item discusses and is strictly worse than this item's residual.\nIt also means the \"every correction to this item narrowed it\" reading -- which\nwas the strongest argument for closing this item -- no longer holds: this\nmechanism is LARGER than filed, which is precisely INV-karud's stated condition\nfor refusing a refined-criterion closure.\n\nSTATUS AND PRIORITY UNCHANGED (violated, P0) pending the owner's disposition."  # 5aa2
- op: discuss  # 0ef7
  at: '2026-08-22T22:28:38Z'  # 0ef7
  by: agent  # 0ef7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0ef7
  clock: 21  # 0ef7
  nonce: 0ef7  # 0ef7
  message: "DISPOSITION BRIEF, evidence RE-RUN AT HEAD (dev 96561cf0f4, post-INV-jujoh\n#480). No ruling is made here; this records the facts the ruling needs so they\ndo not die at compaction. Six fixtures, one net_send must_not_exist claim,\nfs_read control firing in EVERY run.\n\n                                                no overlay   + shipped\n                                                             http overlay\n  f1  requests.post(...) direct                 inconclusive  VIOLATED\n  f2  annotated param session: requests.Session inconclusive  --\n  f3  UNANNOTATED param session.post(...)       CONFIRMED     confirmed_with\n                                                (bare, rc 0)  _caveats\n  f4  OWN __init__ field self.session.post(...) CONFIRMED     confirmed_with\n                                                (bare, rc 0)  _caveats\n  f5  ctor-typed s = requests.Session(); s.post --            inconclusive\n  f6  own field, boto3 upload_fileobj           --            CONFIRMED\n                                                              (bare, rc 0)\n  fx_A own field, STDLIB self.sock.sendall()    confirmed_with_caveats\n\n1) THIS ITEM'S FILED RESIDUAL REPRODUCES VERBATIM. f3 is the shape recorded in\nthe 2026-08-22 correction and still returns bare confirmed at exit 0.\n\n2) THE CAVEAT IS KEYED TO CATALOGUED METHOD-KIND NAMES, read in code\n(untyped_receiver_sites): `boundaries = {p.boundary for p in\ncatalog.lookup_all(name) if p.kind == \"method\" and p.name == name}`; empty ->\nskip. sendall is catalogued (net_send) so it fires with ZERO configuration;\npost is NOT catalogued at all, so it is silent. The function's own docstring\nrecords that the UNSCOPED version was measured 2026-08-11 and marked DO NOT\nBUILD IT.\n\n3) INV-jujoh's FIX IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, verified by a pre/post arm rather than\ninferred: PRE-#480 WITH THE OVERLAY INSTALLED, f4 was still bare confirmed with\n0 caveats. The overlay alone was insufficient -- the emit had to exist first.\n\n4) A NUMBER THAT MUST NOT BE READ THE EASY WAY. Across django/db, mitmproxy,\nmeson, httpx: 17,214 untyped-receiver method sites, 2,403 the caveat can speak\nabout, 14,811 (86.0%) it cannot. THAT IS NOT A HIDDEN-I/O RATE. The top silent\nnames are append(1,048), items(420), extend, add, split, lower, assertEqual --\noverwhelmingly not I/O, and the caveat's silence on them is CORRECT. The live\nresidue is third-party I/O verbs with no catalogue rows (httpx: post 28, json\n62).\n\nTHE CRUX, and it is a scope judgement, not a measurement: does the statement\nquantify over the tool AS SHIPPED WITH DEFAULTS, or over the tool AS CONFIGURED\nper its documented design? Defaults -> the item stays violated. Configured ->\nthe third-party half is answered by the standing ruling (io_primitives stays\nSTDLIB-SCOPED; THIRD-PARTY IN OVERLAYS) and the stdlib half is already\nsatisfied.\n\nTHE ARM THE \"CLOSE IT\" CASE CANNOT ABSORB: f6. With the http overlay INSTALLED,\nboto3 upload_fileobj through an own field STILL returns bare confirmed. So the\nhole is not merely defaulted-off; it is unbounded across libraries, and closing\nit per-library is not closing it. The documented remedy also requires the user\nto declare which libraries perform I/O -- i.e. to already know the answer they\nasked the tool for.\n\nAGENT'S RECOMMENDATION (owner decides): SPLIT rather than answer yes/no. Mark\nthis item satisfied for what it can own and now demonstrably does -- within the\ncatalogue's declared scope a clean verdict is backed by an analysis that could\nhave classified the I/O, and where it could not it says so with no\nconfiguration -- and file the residue as its own item with the sentence it\nactually has: a boundary claim over a library with NO catalogue rows and NO\noverlay returns a bare confirmed through an untyped receiver. That is a split,\nnot a narrow-to-close, so it does not trip INV-karud's bar. If a single answer\nis preferred, the defensible one is NO (stays violated), on f6."  # 0ef7
- op: discuss  # 865b
