  actor: jgstern_agent  # 865b
  clock: 22  # 865b
  nonce: 865b  # 865b
  message: "DISCLOSURE-OPTION MEASUREMENT for the owner's ruling (2026-08-22, 55-min budget,\ndefaults frame). Full data + harness: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/\nmeasurement_inv_fibis_disclosure_options_08222026.md (scratchpad/screen/).\n\nPOPULATION. 289 leaf sub-package scopes x 4 boundary claims = 1,156 pairs:\n1,000 inconclusive / 118 violated / 38 bare confirmed (10 scopes, 3.3%). Selection\nbiases disclosed in the notebook (13 repos; superset+mlflow 37% of first tranche;\nnested dirs; 11 test-named paths; 1 timeout).\n\nOPTIONS SIMULATED post-hoc (no tool change). B = caveat rc 3 whenever ANY\nuntyped-receiver method site exists. D = uncovered-module gate rc 2 when B's\ncondition AND an imported uncatalogued non-analyzed module exists.\n  At HEAD both fire on 30 of 38 bare pairs (other 8 have zero untyped sites).\n  ADJUDICATED 30/30 against source: 0 TRUE POSITIVES. Receivers were str/regex/\n  dict/AST methods, protobuf builders, Django ORM in migrations (caught as\n  VIOLATED on DB-WRITE; fired only on non-DB claims), property plumbing, one\n  ASGIApp (opaque by design).\n  Positive controls through the same harness: f3/f6 fixtures fire B; D names\n  exactly requests / boto3.\n\nPOSITIVE-CONTROL HUNT (fresh agent): NO bare confirmed found on real code. At all\n6 known untyped-receiver I/O sites (litellm client.post x2, mlflow sftp.put,\nfeast conn.execute, airflow session.execute, flink state.put) the gate fired\nfirst; an AST scan of whole_bunch_of_repos found no non-test file that reaches\nI/O only via an uncatalogued-name untyped receiver while calling no\nnon-enumerated module. Corpus-coverage statement, not proof.\n\nREFUTER PANEL (fresh agent): B extraction == shipped population (0/33,532\ndiscrepant). D's import trigger names the scope's OWN sibling files at\nsub-package scope (meson: 12 of 13) -- a D precision defect. Refuter's \"first-\nparty exclusion fails\" claim REFUTED on re-check: all 28 third-party-free\ninconclusives name PARENT-PACKAGE modules not read at that scope, 0 in-scope.\n\nNOISE FLOORS. B: 11,971 untyped sites, 34.7% builtin container/str methods,\n3.6% I/O-verb-shaped. Gate: median 12 uncovered modules per inconclusive scope\n(p90 33), mostly parent-package + torch/numpy/PIL + un-enumerated stdlib\n(atexit, binascii).\n\nRULE-19 CEILING. Of 1,000 inconclusive pairs, 98% have untyped sites and 22%\nhave I/O-verb-shaped ones. D goes SILENT once a module is catalogued (protection\npasses to the method-name caveat, conditional on the overlay listing that\nmethod). B does not erode.\n\nOwner decides. Status/priority untouched."  # 865b
- op: discuss  # 1c3e
  at: '2026-08-23T01:30:11Z'  # 1c3e
  by: agent  # 1c3e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1c3e
  clock: 23  # 1c3e
  nonce: 1c3e  # 1c3e
  message: "*** POSITIVE CONTROL FOUND ON REAL CODE. *** Corpus-wide hunt, 2026-08-22\n01:14-01:30 UTC. Full data: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/\nmeasurement_inv_fibis_positive_control_08222026.md\n\nMETHOD. AST scan of 32,593 non-test .py files for the shape that can produce a\nbare confirmed: an I/O verb NOT among the 120 catalogued method-kind names (so\nthe untyped_receiver caveat structurally CANNOT fire) called on a receiver the\nanalyzer cannot type. 273 files hit -> 214 directory scopes -> verify-claims on\nall 214 (856 pairs).\n\nRESULT 1 -- NO NATURALLY-OCCURRING FALSE CONFIRMED, which confirms the earlier\nfinding rather than overturning it. 719 inconclusive / 177 violated / 8 bare\nconfirmed, and all 8 are antlr3 DFA `predict` in vendored parser copies --\ngenuinely not I/O. With no overlay, the gate holds today.\n\nRESULT 2 -- BUT THE PROTECTION IS ENTIRELY BORROWED, AND NEVER THIS ITEM'S OWN\nMECHANISM. 90 scopes carry a real untyped-receiver uncatalogued-verb I/O site\n(post 56, upload_file 6, upload 6, put_item/get_item 6, download_file 5,\nexecute_command 3, delete_object 3, download_blob/upload_blob 2, patch 2):\n    protected by the uncatalogued-module gate .... 68\n    protected by opaque-launch ................... 13\n    protected by unsupported-language ............. 5\n    already violated .............................. 4\n    PROTECTED BY THE untyped_receiver CAVEAT ...... 0\nOption A fires on NONE of them. Every protecting mechanism is a coverage gap the\nproject intends to close. Seven scopes are <=3 named modules from a bare\nconfirmed: polis/deploy (2), airflow providers alibaba / apache.hdfs /\nmicrosoft.azure (2 each), ClickHouse utils/backupview (3).\n\nRESULT 3 -- THE DEMONSTRATION, on unmodified real code.\nspecial_repos/polis/deploy/deploy-static-assets.py, a CLI whose purpose is\nuploading static assets to S3:\n    line 31  def upload_file(s3_client, file_path, bucket, base_path):  # UNANNOTATED\n    line 60  s3_client.upload_file(str(file_path), bucket, relative_path, ...)\n    line 74  s3_client = boto3.client(\"s3\")\n  no overlay ............................. rc 2 inconclusive (boto3, mimetypes)\n  realistic overlay OMITTING upload_file . rc 0 \"never sends data over the\n                                           network: CONFIRMED\"  <-- FALSE\n  same overlay LISTING upload_file ....... rc 3 confirmed_with_caveats naming\n                                           deploy-static-assets.py:60\n\nTHE CONDITION, STATED PRECISELY SO NOBODY OVERREADS THIS: the false confirm\nrequires the overlay to declare `module_completeness: boto3 complete` -- which is\nexactly how a user escapes `inconclusive` -- while its primitive rows omit\nupload_file. That is a user over-claim the tool cannot detect and actively\nrewards. A primitives-only overlay without the completeness declaration still\nreturns inconclusive (tested).\n\nWHAT IT SETTLES. The documented remedy for the third-party half of this item\n(overlays, INV-fotav) is the very thing that removes the accidental protection\nfor the untyped-receiver half. Rule 19's anti-correlation is no longer a\nprojection about future coverage: a user following the CURRENT documented advice\ngets the false certification TODAY. My earlier \"B but not yet\" rested on the\nexposure being hypothetical. It is not. I withdraw the \"not yet\"."  # 1c3e
