  message: "*** OPTION B IMPLEMENTED AND MERGED (PR #481, dev aa7e878572). *** The owner\ndirected \"implement B\" after the positive control. Behavioral evidence re-run on\nthe MERGED tree with fresh caches, not a proxy:\n\n  polis/deploy + the realistic incomplete overlay\n      BEFORE  rc 0  \"never sends data over the network: confirmed\"\n      AFTER   rc 3  confirmed_with_caveats, CAVEAT (unknown_receiver_scope):\n              \"At 4 of 11 method call site(s) the receiver's type could not be\n              determined ... distinct method(s): get, is_file, items,\n              upload_file.\"\n  f3 (session.post via unannotated param, NO overlay)\n      confirmed -> confirmed_with_caveats\n  FALSIFIABILITY CONTROL (all receivers typed: p: pathlib.Path -> p.read_text())\n      rc 0, verdict confirmed, ZERO caveats   <-- the guarantee is still capable\n                                                  of being clean\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. New caveat kind `unknown_receiver_scope` carrying a COUNT, a\nDENOMINATOR and the DISTINCT METHOD NAMES. It is deliberately UNSCOPED, because\nmatching the callee's name against the catalogue is exactly what an untyped\nreceiver makes meaningless -- the 90-scopes-to-zero measurement. It QUALIFIES\nrather than WITHHOLDS, so the 2026-08-11 refusal of the unscoped DOWNGRADE\nstands untouched and is cited in the code.\n\nTESTS THAT PINNED THE OLD DECISION WERE INVERTED, NOT DELETED.\nTestTheResidualThisDoesNotClose (\"a PR that changes it should be closing\nINV-fibis, not passing by\") is now TestTheResidualNowClosed and carries the old\nargument in full: its PREMISE survives -- there is no signal distinguishing\nsession.post from items.append -- and its CONCLUSION does not, because a call on\nan object of unknown type is not evidence of ABSENCE either, and must_not_exist\nis an assertion about absence. Three boundary-scoping tests were NARROWED to the\nguarantee that actually survives (no boundary-SPECIFIC claim about an unrelated\n.get), not weakened.\n\nCONSUMER IMPACT, stated plainly: claims that exited 0 may now exit 3. No envelope\nbump (a new caveat kind is additive), but a gate written `verify-claims || exit\n1` fails where it passed. Spec updated. Also refactored: the four clean-verdict\npaths now build their caveat list through ONE builder, so a future disclosure\ncannot be attached to three of them and forgotten on the fourth.\n\n*** THIS ITEM IS NOT CLOSED, AND HERE IS WHAT IS LEFT. *** B closed the\nDISCLOSURE gap. The statement also has a RECALL half that is untouched:\nexternal_field_types (an own field of external type still resolves to nothing),\nand extending call-site parameter typing to __init__ params that become own\nfields. Neither is blocked by anything; both are authorised under the standing\nINV-fibis chain ruling. And the DISPOSITION question I put to the owner is still\nopen and is now better posed: with the closed-world disclosure shipped, does\n\"every clean confirmed is backed by an analysis that COULD have classified the\nI/O\" now hold -- given that the analysis still cannot classify it, but no longer\nclaims to have? Status and priority left UNCHANGED (violated, P0) pending that."  # 7cec
- op: discuss  # 504e
  at: '2026-08-23T05:57:16Z'  # 504e
  by: agent  # 504e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 504e
  clock: 25  # 504e
  nonce: 504e  # 504e
  message: "OWNER DIRECTION 2026-08-23, in their words: \"we should move forward with\nINV-fibis/INV-nuhun under the assumption that we will add pyright etc in due\ncourse.\"\n\nWHAT THIS SETTLES. This item is NOT BLOCKED on multi-fidelity receiver typing\nand must not be held waiting for it. Filed as WI-nanom (Python pyright/SCIP\nbackend, ADR-0012 coexistence, spec section 20 -- the same shape already\nshipped for Rust via rust-analyzer). No isbefore edge exists in either\ndirection, deliberately: the dependency is an ASSUMPTION about the future, not\na prerequisite.\n\nWHY IT CANNOT BE A PREREQUISITE, which is what prompted the direction. This\nitem is about the RESIDUAL -- a clean verdict must be honest about the\nreceivers it CANNOT type. A language-server backend SHRINKS that set and never\nempties it: **kwargs, getattr, values out of json.loads, C extensions without\nstubs, untyped third-party packages. Measured against the open set on\n2026-08-23, WI-nanom likely closes INV-mumov and probably WI-sitos / WI-jojuv,\ndents INV-linub and WI-makij, and moves THIS item not at all. Waiting for it\nwould be waiting for something that was never going to arrive.\n\nWHAT IT DOES DO, labelled as a separate thing rather than blurred in: it cuts\nthe disclosure VOLUME sharply. On hypergumbo's own tree at dev 30370c4cd6,\n6,541 of 9,267 method call sites (70.6%) have an untypeable receiver. Every\nreceiver typed is one this item's caveat need not raise, so that ratio is the\nrecall scoreboard -- and it cannot be gamed by adding catalogue rows.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED (violated) pending the one question still outstanding, which\nis NOT the pyright question and is shared verbatim with the sibling item: does\n\"backed by an analysis that COULD HAVE classified/constructed the flow\" hold\nwhen the analysis still cannot, but no longer claims to have? A third option\nwas put to the owner and is still live -- that the statement as written demands\nsomething no static tool ever achieves, so the right move may be to REWRITE THE\nBAR rather than to rule the current wording satisfied or violated.\n\nNEXT WORK, unblocked and proceeding: the RECALL half -- external_field_types,\nand extending call-site parameter typing to __init__ params that become own\nfields. Authorised under the standing INV-fibis chain ruling, discharges both\nitems' shared mechanism, and needs nothing from WI-nanom."  # 504e
